
======================================================================================
A.  The two potentials:  ds^2 = -(1+2Psi/c^2)c^2dt^2 + (1-2Phi/c^2)(dr^2+r^2 dOmega^2)
======================================================================================
  linearized Einstein tensor, mixed components, first order in the metric perturbation:
    G^0_0                 = -2 lap(Phi)/c^2                      [residual 0]
    G^r_r - G^theta_theta = (1/c^2)[(Phi-Psi)'' - (Phi-Psi)'/r]  [residual 0]
    G^r_r + 2 G^theta_theta = -(2/c^2) lap(Phi-Psi)              [residual 0]
  (all three residuals are exactly 0: the identities are certified by sympy)

  Einstein equations  G^mu_nu = (8 pi G/c^4) T^mu_nu  with  T^mu_nu = diag(-rho c^2, p_r, p_t, p_t):

    (i)    lap(Phi)                       = 4 pi G rho                     [Poisson; Phi is the spatial potential]
    (ii)   (Phi-Psi)'' - (Phi-Psi)'/r     = (8 pi G/c^2)(p_r - p_t)        [traceless / anisotropic part]
    (iii)  lap(Phi - Psi)                 = -4 pi G (p_r + 2 p_t)/c^2      [trace part]

  adding (i) and (iii):

    (iv)   lap[(Phi+Psi)/2] = 4 pi G [ rho + (p_r + 2 p_t)/(2 c^2) ]   <-- THE LENSING SOURCE
    (v)    lap(Psi)         = 4 pi G [ rho + (p_r + 2 p_t)/c^2     ]   <-- THE TOLMAN / ACTIVE SOURCE

  A1  the photon.  Null geodesic of the gauge above:  c dt = n dl with
      n = sqrt((1-2Phi/c^2)/(1+2Psi/c^2)) = 1 - (Phi+Psi)/c^2 + O(c^-4),
      so the deflection is governed by (Phi+Psi) and
      kappa = Sigma_eff/Sigma_crit,  Sigma_eff = INT [ rho + (p_r+2p_t)/(2c^2) ] dz.
  A2  PPN cross-check of the factor 1/2 (independent of the linearized step).
      GR PPN, static perfect fluid:  -g_00 = 1-2U+2U^2-6 Phi_4 + 2 Phi_2,  g_ij = (1+2U) delta_ij
      n - 1 = -Phi_2 + 3*Phi_4 + 2*U  +  3*Phi_2**2/2 - 9*Phi_2*Phi_4 - 4*Phi_2*U + 27*Phi_4**2/2 + 12*Phi_4*U + U**2  + O(3)
      with lap(U) = -4 pi G rho and lap(Phi_4) = -4 pi G p, the pressure enters n-1 as 3 Phi_4
      against 2U:  fractional correction to the lensing source = 3p/(2 rho c^2).
      Formula (iv) with p_r = p_t = p gives exactly (p_r+2p_t)/(2 rho c^2) = 3p/(2 rho c^2).  MATCH.
      (The other 1PN terms, -U^2 and -Phi_2, are of the same order |Phi_N|/c^2 and are NOT
       anisotropic-stress corrections; they are reported, not claimed, in section D.)

======================================================================================
B.  The law's halo:  u = (1+sqrt(1+4x^2))/(2x^2),  x = r/r_M,  r_M = sqrt(G M_b/a0)
======================================================================================
  B1  KA1 equilibrium (momentum conservation):  dPi_rr/dr + (2/r)(Pi_rr-Pi_tt) + rho_h g
      in units (a0^2/4 pi G)/r_M, symbolic  =  0
      -> the stress is EXACTLY in equilibrium with the weight of the phantom halo it holds.
      -> consequence: given Pi_ij, momentum balance FIXES the density: rho_medium = rho_h.
         The stress and the mass are not independent knobs.
  B2  asymptotics at x -> infinity, w = 1/x, units v_inf^2/(4 pi):
        sigma_t^2 = Pi_tt/rho_h :  2*pi + 2*pi*w/3 + pi*w**2/4 + pi*w**3/30 + O(w**4)
        sigma_r^2 = Pi_rr/rho_h :  -2*pi + 2*pi*w/3 - pi*w**2/4 + pi*w**3/30 + O(w**4)
        (Pi_rr+Pi_tt)/Pi_tt     :  2*w/3 - 2*w**2/9 + O(w**3)
      deep field (x -> infinity):
        sigma_t^2 -> +v_inf^2/2   [+2 pi in the units above]
        sigma_r^2 -> -v_inf^2/2   [-2 pi in the units above]
        (Pi_rr+Pi_tt)/Pi_tt -> 0 as 2/(3x) - 2/(9x^2) + ...  (6.64e-03 at x = 100)
      exact limits:  sigma_t^2/(v_inf^2/2) -> 1 ,  sigma_r^2/(v_inf^2/2) -> -1
      with v_inf^4 = G M_b a0.  The radial "dispersion" is NEGATIVE: no kinetic gas can do it.

