  M1  gas instead of a solid: p_r = +p_t = rho sigma^2 (no tension).  Then
      p_r + 2 p_t = 3 rho sigma^2 and the lensing correction is 3 sigma^2/(2c^2):
      at most 3 x the tabulated column, i.e. <= 6.7e-06 at log M_b 11.  The SIGN of p_r
      is not what carries the verdict: the magnitude is.
  M2  Tolman factor 1 instead of 1/2: 2x.  M3  |p_r|+2|p_t|: 3x.  Both in D3; both fail.
  M4  narrower denominators (excess over the budget / over the delivered charge): in D3.
      The narrowest denominator, over the charge that falls in, is 3.8x the widest at
      x = 10 and still 5 orders of magnitude short.
  M5  extended baryons (Hernquist, a_h = 0.05 / 0.2 / 0.5 r_M) instead of a point mass.
      The point-mass profiles are singular at x -> 0 (rho_h ~ 1/x, sigma_t^2 ~ 1/x) so the
      ratio at small x is an artefact; the extended runs in D5 bound the true inner value.
      Result: the artefact is removed, R -> 0 at the centre, and the maximum over the whole
      of 0 < x <= 10 is 2.3054e-06 (canonical) / 2.5344e-06 (alt) -- the number the label is read from.

